## readme
## ### Before you start
## 
## Before you begin, make sure you meet these prerequisites:  
## 
## * Bash >= 5.2
## 
## ### Get started
## 
## 1) Download: `git clone git+ssh://pi@rpi400.local/srv/repo/git/pads.git`
## 
## 2) Install: `makepkg -si`
## 
## 3) Add to /etc/pacman.conf:
## ```bash
## [datasphere]
## SigLevel = Optional TrustAll
## Server = http://rpi400.local/db/core
## ```
## 
## ### What's next
## 
## end readme

## exit
## 0   | Success
## 1   | Failure
## 127 | K18
## 130 | Ctl+C
## end exit

## env
## NA | NA
## end env

## file
## \${baseDir}/docs | Documentation generated by [paddocs][#paddocs]
## \${baseDir}/packaging | PKGBUILD Files
## \${baseDir}/source/bin | Executable Directory
## \${baseDir}/source/pads | Libraries used by PADS
## \${baseDir}/tests | Run tests, etc.
## end file

## module
## -B | Compile lib into a distribute
## -C | Create new dev env's and files
## -D | Dryrun
## -T | Make files from templates
## -U | Update local repo at `/srv/repo/db/core`
## -x | Set -x
## end module

## api
## build.sh  | -B | -[<p>] <name> | 0 success 1 error | Src Code for logic in build scripts
## create.sh | -C | -[<d,f>] \<name>   | 0 Success 1 Error | Src Code for logic in managing projects
## templates.sh | -T | -[<p,i,c,m,l,x>] <name> | 0 Success 1 Error | Src Code for build templates
## update.sh | -U | -{<r>} <name> | 0 Success 1 Error | Src Code for updating local repo
## end api

## example
## `pads -Cd /path/to/dev/env assets etc config docs`
## : Make a new Development Env with the directories `assets`, `etc`, `config` and `docs`. The directory structure can also be stored in a text file.

## `pads -Cd /path/to/dev/env/shcmd docs packaging source/bin`
## : Make a new bash command. This could be any lang. The directory structure can also be stored in a text file.

## `pads -Cf /path/to/dev/env/shcmd CHANGELOG.md README.md LICENSE`
## : Make any files needed for the lib. This can be any file in any directory. The file structure can also be stored in a text file.

## `pads -Tc shcmd > /path/to/dev/env/shcmd/source/bin/shcmd`
## : Make a new bin file with the proper headers and getops, etc. The default output is the terminal, it must be piped to a file.

## `pads -Tp shcmd > /path/to/dev/env/shcmd/packaging/PKGBUILD`
## : Make a PKGBUILD file for a give cmd. The default output is the terminal, it must be piped to a file.

## `pads -Bp shcmd`
## : Build the lib into a distribute, or official release. Built in `shcmd/packaging`.

## `pads -Ur shcmd`
## : Update the local repo located at `/srv/repo/core`.
## end example

## advanced
## `pads -Cd dirStructure.txt`
## : You can design your directory structure in a plain text file that can be interpereted by `mkdir -p`. Which also means you can build dirs, and subdirs anyway that be read by bash. (eg: path/to/{{nested/dirs,or/aother/dir},yet/another/{confusing,nested,dir}})

## `pads -Cf fileStructure.txt`
## : You can design your file structure in a plain text file that can be interpereted by `touch`. Which means you can build the files using any bashism you can think of. (eg: path/to/{CHANGLOG,README}.md)
## end advanced

